# SBK and sbk-charts release coordinates used by sbk-analytics.
#
# Each project is identified by a (URL, version) pair:
#   <project>.url     - GitHub repository URL (or 'owner/repo' shorthand)
#   <project>.version - release tag that must exist on that repository
#
# SBK 10.0 launches Java via the SBK_JAVA_HOME environment variable.
# sbk-analytics resolves a JDK whose major version matches `sbk.jdk.version`
# by probing (in order):
#   1. an already-cached download under ~/.cache/sbk-analytics/jdk/<ver>/
#   2. SBK_JAVA_HOME    (exported by the user)
#   3. JAVA_HOME        (exported by the user)
#   4. `java` on PATH
# Only if none of those match does it download Temurin of that major version
# from Adoptium. The chosen JDK home is then exported as SBK_JAVA_HOME
# (NOT SBK_JDK_HOME) for every sbk-yal / sbk-gem-yal invocation.

sbk.url=https://github.com/kmgowda/SBK
sbk.version=10.0
sbk.jdk.version=25

sbk-charts.url=https://github.com/kmgowda/sbk-charts
sbk-charts.version=4.26.6.1
